{"changes":["(New) Import a playlist from a USB device into your collection, matching existing tracks and optionally copying missing music.","(New) Choose how Import Playlist handles missing device tracks: copy them, ask each time, import matched tracks only, or cancel.","(New) Choose whether a dropped folder that conflicts with a playlist is copied, replaced, kept, or confirmed; replacements clearly report what was removed.","(New) Import and export star ratings with USB devices.","(New) Choose the BPM range used when analysing tracks and imports.","(New) Show and sort by each track’s file creation date in the library browser.","(New) Optionally write edited track keys to audio-file tags.","(New) Create Intelligent Playlists from the playlist tree menus.","(New) Select or clear every playlist at once in Sync Manager.","(New) Continue through a playlist when a track ends in 1 PLAYER or SIMPLE PLAYER, and use the player’s previous and next controls to move through its loaded list.","(New) See saved and active loops marked in the MEMORY list and waveform overview.","(New) Change a hot cue’s colour from its pad and clear a set pad directly.","(New) Choose whether adding a track already on a USB playlist adds another copy or skips it.","(New) Locate the track loaded on a deck and restore its list position.","(New) Reorder long playlists by dragging at the track list’s edges to scroll.","(New) Install and run rbxport through Nix on Linux.","(Fixed) Analysis respects the current first-beat memory-cue preference, including when preferences are changed in another rbxport window.","(Fixed) Cloud-synced tracks can play from their Dropbox copy when their original file is gone, including after restarting rbxport.","(Fixed) Command+Q no longer selects all tracks on AZERTY keyboard layouts.","(Fixed) rbxport still shows its window if its page cannot load.","(Fixed) XDJ-RX3 LINK connections work more reliably on Linux, including automatic joining and hot-cue colours.","(Fixed) USB exports are more compatible with older players and retain distinct same-named playlists and their tracks.","(Fixed) BPM analysis keeps measured tempos accurately and analyses Normal mode as a constant tempo.","(Fixed) Explorer shows mapped drives, and Windows can drop MP3 files onto playlists.","(Fixed) USB tracks whose file-path case differs from the drive can play on Linux.","(Fixed) Artwork loads from supported network shares and linked library paths.","(Fixed) Auto Relocate can find moved files elsewhere on their original drive and in more search locations.","(Fixed) Linked players can load library tracks stored through supported symbolic-link paths.","(Fixed) Cancelling a dropped-folder conflict leaves that folder untouched, and a failed replacement cannot leave a partial playlist change.","(Improved) Large dropped-folder imports spend less time holding the library write lock."]}
